rch complements and expands the department's existing strengths. The successful candidate will teach undergraduate and graduate courses in biological psychology and neuroscience, establish a research program that actively involves undergraduate and master's students, and demonstrates the potential to secure external\nfunding that supports research and student training. \n\nThe department offers dedicated laboratory space, specialized equipment, and facilities supporting both human and non-human animal research, providing an excellent environment for developing an independent research program and interdisciplinary collaborations. We seek a colleague committed to outstanding teaching, inclusive mentorship, and fostering the academic and professional success of our diverse student population. A Ph.D. in psychology, neuroscience, biology, or a related area is required at the time of appointment. The expected start date for the position is August 16, 2027. Case Aide/ vCSRI (UEC) San Bernardino - San Bernardino Campus The Case Aide plays a vital role in supporting the mission of the Cal State Reentry Initiative (CSRI) by assisting participants in their transition and reintegration into the community. Under the general supervision of the Center Manager, the Case Aide works independently and collaboratively to provide administrative support, monitor participant progress, and\nassist in case management functions. This position requires strong communication, organizational skills, and a commitment to fostering a positive, prosocial environment for participants. Security Guard/CSRI Indio (UEC) San Bernardino - San Bernardino Campus The Security Guard is responsible for maintaining a safe and secure environment at the CSRI center while also assisting with clerical tasks, monitoring surveillance cameras, and engaging in participant outreach. This role ensures the safety of staff, clients, and visitors, while also supporting administrative functions and fostering a welcoming atmosphere for program participants. Academic Success & Undergraduate Advising (ASUA), Student Success Studio (S3) Mentor - Student Assistant, Palm Desert Campus San Bernardino - Palm Desert Campus 1 Oct 2026 Palm Desert Campus. Admitted/enrolled CSU, San Bernardino students are eligible to apply for student employment positions. College of Arts & Letters, Coyote Radio & Advertising, Graphic Designer - Student Assistant San Bernardino - San Bernardino Campus 30 Sep 2026 Admitted/enrolled CSU, San Bernardino students are eligible to apply for student employment positions Robert and Frances Fullerton Museum of Art, Graphic Design - Student Assistant San Bernardino - San Bernardino Campus 30 Sep 2026 Admitted/enrolled CSU, San Bernardino students are eligible to apply for student employment positions Library - Federal Work Study Student Assistant, Palm Desert Campus San Bernardino - Palm Desert Campus 30 Sep 2026 Palm Desert Campus Position. Federal Work Study Position. Enrolled CSU, San Bernardino students are eligible to apply for student employment positions. Reprographics Specialist (Reprographics Specialist II), Support Services San Bernardino - San Bernardino Campus 15 Sep 2026 The purpose of this position is to support the department and campus community by producing printed materials efficiently and in a timely manner using a variety of print methods including digital printing (black and white, color, and envelope printing) and large format printing, as well as various bindery and finishing techniques for a polished, finished product. Project Coordinator/SOP ICDFR (UEC) San Bernardino - San Bernardino Campus The part-time Project Coordinator will help manage the daily work of the SOP parenting program. This position will schedule classes, work with schools and community sites, recruit families, supervise parent educators, and train/supervise student staff. The coordinator will also prepare program materials, track attendance, maintain records, and make sure classes