Palm Desert Campus Site Header Region CSUSB Home We Define the Future Apply Visit Request Info myCoyote PDC Give Search CSUSB Search CSUSB CSUSB Main Menu Page Header Career Center Page Menu About Us Expand Menu Item About Us FAQs Meet Our Team Hours & Locations Our Impact Alumni Employers/Partners Expand Menu Item Employers/Partners Handshake / Post a Job Career Fairs Internships Engagement Opportunities Employer Policies Partners Program Cody's Closet Gift in Kind Handshake Students Expand Menu Item Students Career Resources Major and Career Exploration Prepare for Graduate School Job/Internship Search Resumes, Cover Letters & CV's Interview Preparation Clothing Resources Cross-Cultural Career Resources & FAQs Events Staff/Faculty Expand Menu Item Staff/Faculty Posting student on-campus Jobs Handshake Video Library Presentation Request Work Local Main Content Region Career Center Visit the Career Center! (8am-5:00pm) Drop-in Hours! ( Sep 1st - Nov 25th) Get personalized career advising, resume and cover letter support, internship and job search help, and grad school planning—all in one place. Stop by during drop-in hours or visit us in person to start building your future this Spring. San Bernardino: Tues & Thurs :11am - 1PM; 3pm-5pm | Wednesday 11am-1pm Palm Desert: Wednesday 11am-1pm 📍 SB Campus Location: SMSU South 112 📍 PDC Location: IW 102 Career Readiness Summer 2026 Workshops! Build-up your success in the workplace this summer with our 6-part professional development workshop series. From exploring career options to crafting resumes & navigating the job search, confidently launch into your dream career! Virtual ZOOM: 12pm-12:50pm Virtual Link Book an Appointment with our Career Counselors! We’re your Career Center team, and we’re here to support you every step of the way. Whether you’re exploring career options, getting involved in hands-on experiences, or preparing for life after graduation, we’re here to help. Through personalized support, engaging programs, and real-world learning opportunities, we work alongside students and recent alumni to build confidence, career readiness, and meaningful connections, all while staying true to CSUSB’s commitment to student success and community engagement. Book an appointment today with our Career Counselors! Navigate Appointment! SAVE THE DATE: Career Fairs/ Lunch and Learns! Join the CSUSB Career Center for an exciting lineup of Fall 2026 events! Connect with employers, explore career and graduate school opportunities, prepare for upcoming fairs, and build valuable professional skills. Events are open to students of all majors and alumni . RSVP today to reserve your spot! RSVP HERE! Our Mission Empowering students and recent alumni, the CSUSB Career Center is dedicated to fostering a comprehensive career readiness skill set that aligns with the evolving global market. Through a blend of exploration, tailored programming, and immersive experiential learning, we guide individuals in achieving their personal and professional aspirations while staying true to the spirit of CSUSB's commitment to student success, research, and regional engagement. By nurturing the holistic growth—professionally, ethically, and intellectually—of our students, alumni, faculty, and staff, we actively promote inclusive environments across industries. Overview of Services Handout About Enterprise Mobility JOIN TO START YOUR JOURNEY. Stay to see where the journey takes you. Whether you’re looking for constant growth and development, impactful work, opportunities for promotion, or colleagues you can have fun with along the way, you’ll find it at Enterprise Mobility. Just bring your enthusiasm, talent and team spirit, and we’ll provide the resources to support you. Learn More Enterprise Mobility Careers About Caltrans From backroads to busy freeways, Caltrans keeps California moving. We manage 50,000+ miles of highways, support rail, permit 400+ airports, and partner locally to connect communities with exciting opportunities from engineering to admin. We improve lives through transportation to support a thriving, connected California. Join us in building a safer, stronger, more sustainable future! Learn More About Caltrans About Think Together Founded in 1997, Think Together partners with schools to change the odds for kids by providing award-winning programs during and outside the school day. We’re one of California’s largest nonprofits working in school districts from San Diego to San Francisco. Whether you’re interested in early learning, elementary, middle or high school, you can invest in your community by working at a local school or working within our home office providing support! Learn More About Think Together Thank You Partners To our incredible CSUSB Career Center Partners, A huge THANK YOU! Your commitment to CSUSB students is truly inspiring. Because of your partnership, our students are gaining the real-world experience and professional connections they need to succeed. Whether you've hired an intern, participated in a career fair, or shared your expertise, you've helped us bridge the gap between education and career. We couldn't do it without your support! Cheers to a successful partnership! Best, The CSUSB Career Center Team About Ensemble Therapy Ensemble Therapy offers a wide variety of therapy options for all ages. We provide both in-person and virtual care in clinic and school settings, ensuring easy accessibility. Our services include Speech Therapy, Occupational Therapy, Physical Therapy, ABA Therapy, Mental Health, and more. Come join our team! Learn More About Ensemble Therapy About Inland Regional Energy Network I-REN is a coalition of three regional agencies and 54 public agencies across Riverside and San Bernardino Counties, working to advance California’s clean energy initiatives. Its mission is to strengthen the clean energy economy by building local government capacity, developing a skilled energy-efficiency workforce, and supporting long-term energy code compliance in collaboration with building departments and industry partners. Learn More About Inland Regional Energy Network Career Advising Resumes, Cover Letters, & CVs Graduate School Prep Job & Internship Search HACU Conference Award Explore Majors & Careers Meet Our Team March 20, 2023 Dr. Tiffany Bitting Director | Liaison to Academic Affairs, Basic Needs, Children's Center, Student Conduct and Ethical Development March 20, 2023 Valentina Felix, M. A. Career Counselor | Liaison to College of Natural Sciences, Services to Students with Disabilities, ASI, SMSU, and ASUA March 20, 2023 Oscar Fonseca, M.S. Career Readiness Program Coordinator | Liaison to Palm Desert Campus, Ed Talent Search, First Star Academy, Gear Up, Upward Bound, and University Honors Program March 20, 2023 Sarai Maldonado, M. B. A. Career Counselor | Liaison to College of Arts & Letters, Veterans Success Center, Undocumented Student Success Center, EOP, and SAIL May 17, 2023 Lauren Williams, M.S., PPS Career Counselor | Liaison to College of Social and Behavioral Sciences, Athletics, Office of Black Student Success, and Housing and Residential Education June 5, 2023 Maricarmen Martinez-Solano, B.S. Career Counselor | Liaison to College of Education & Pre-Professional Programs, CAPS, Rec and Wellness, Student Health Center, The Retreat, and Admissions and Outreach March 20, 2023 Kathy Xu, M.B.A. Budget Analyst June 5, 2023 David Hernandez, BA Event Coordinator November 24, 2025 Vacant Employer Relations Coordinator In order to use Ask Cody you must accept functional cookies. Right Content Make a Gift Career Coach Internship Coyote Connection Contact Us Career Center Email careercenter@csusb.edu Phone Number (909) 537-5250 Location: SUS-112 Office Hours Monday - Friday: 8:00 am-5:00 pm Saturday - Sunday: Closed SUMMER OFFICE HOURS San Bernardino & Palm Desert Campus Monday through Thursday from 7:00 am - 5:30 pm _______________________ Palm Desert Campus Hours: Monday through Friday from 8:00 am - 5:00 pm Location: IW-106 Phone: (909) 537-8243 Email: pdccareercenter@csusb.edu _______________________ CONNECT WITH US: Make An Appointment Footer Region CSUSB California State University, San Bernardino 5500 University Parkway San Bernardino, CA 92407 +1 (909) 537-5000 Follow Us CSUSB's Facebook CSUSB's Twitter CSUSB's YouTube CSUSB's Instagram CSUSB's TikTok CSUSB's LinkedIn CSUSB's Social Media CSUSB Palm Desert Campus 37500 Cook Street Palm Desert, CA 92211 +1 (760) 341-2883 Follow Us PDC's Facebook PDC's YouTube PDC's Instagram Column 1 Login myCoyote Login Canvas Student Email Login Faculty & Staff Email Login Drupal Login Of Interest to... Future Students Current Students Interests Faculty & Staff Interests Full-Time Faculty Interests Part-Time Faculty Interests Community & Visitors Interests Alumni & Friends University Partners Interests Military/Veterans Interests Column 2 Employment CSUSB Job Listings - CSUSB Faculty Jobs - CSUSB Career Center - CSUSB Human Resources - CSUSB Student Employment Federal Work Study Resources Contact CSUSB Clery Act Annual Security Report Annual Fire Safety Report Title IX Notice - CSUSB Disclosure of Consumer Information - CSUSB Column 3 Campus Services Academic Advising - CSUSB Housing & Residential Life - CSUSB Parenting Students Parking - CSUSB Police - CSUSB Psychological Counseling - CSUSB Services to Students with Disabilities - CSUSB Student Health Center - CSUSB Technology Support Transcripts - CSUSB Accessibility Privacy and Security Non-Discrimination Notice Website Copyright/DMCA Policy"
